# LLT display format output formatter — dependency-chain contract.
#
# Converts each value to its LLT representation string: e.g. 42, "hello", [0: 1  ...], etc.
# Uses the llt-repr builtin which traverses and formats the value, materializing nested thunks on demand.
#
# Chain: flush(written) depends on written which depends on llt-repr(%), creating
# a dependency chain that forces everything when materialize() is called on loader's final thunk.

--- uses: ["async"]
[written: [if [seq? %]
  [reduce [fn [let h x] [write [str [llt-repr x] "\n"] h]] %stdout %]
  [write [str [llt-repr %] "\n"] %stdout]]]

[flush written]
